 "cues": [
  {
   "s": 0.5,
   "e": 2.84,
   "text": "Here's a pretty normal DeFi request:"
  },
  {
   "s": 2.88,
   "e": 7.113,
   "text": "stake ETH with Lido and borrow USDC against it on Aave."
  },
  {
   "s": 7.153,
   "e": 11.113,
   "text": "And the same on Solana, with Marinade and Kamino."
  },
  {
   "s": 13.163,
   "e": 16.072,
   "text": "On the left is Claude Code with no harness."
  },
  {
   "s": 16.112,
   "e": 19.776,
   "text": "It has to go find the contract addresses, fetch the ABIs,"
  },
  {
   "s": 19.816,
   "e": 23.293,
   "text": "ask you for an RPC endpoint, and write its own script."
  },
  {
   "s": 23.333,
   "e": 25.871,
   "text": "Then it hits a revert, error 27,"
  },
  {
   "s": 25.911,
   "e": 31.153,
   "text": "because Aave actually takes wstETH, not stETH."
  },
  {
   "s": 31.193,
   "e": 35.379,
   "text": "And then it asks for your private key in a .env file."
  },
  {
   "s": 35.419,
   "e": 38.433,
   "text": "On the right it's the same model, through Aomi."
  },
  {
   "s": 38.473,
   "e": 41.022,
   "text": "It reads the wrap rate, simulates the stake,"
  },
  {
   "s": 41.062,
   "e": 42.288,
   "text": "checks the loan-to-value,"
  },
  {
   "s": 42.328,
   "e": 46.532,
   "text": "and all six steps pass on a fork as one bundle."
  },
  {
   "s": 47.082,
   "e": 50.258,
   "text": "On Solana it's the same story with different failures:"
  },
  {
   "s": 50.298,
   "e": 52.011,
   "text": "a rate-limited RPC,"
  },
  {
   "s": 52.051,
   "e": 54.786,
   "text": "a missing token account, Kamino's refresh rule,"
  },
  {
   "s": 54.826,
   "e": 56.876,
   "text": "and the transaction size limit."
  },
  {
   "s": 56.916,
   "e": 59.023,
   "text": "Aomi simulates it all in Lite"
  },
  {
   "s": 59.063,
   "e": 62.85,
   "text": "S V M and sends one transaction."
  },
  {
   "s": 63.1,
   "e": 65.254,
   "text": "The point of having a harness is performance,"
  },
  {
   "s": 65.294,
   "e": 67.541,
   "text": "token efficiency, and security."
  },
  {
   "s": 67.581,
   "e": 70.107,
   "text": "A lot of people argue frontier models"
  },
  {
   "s": 70.147,
   "e": 72.139,
   "text": "can transact without any harness,"
  },
  {
   "s": 72.179,
   "e": 73.3,
   "text": "and they kind of can."
  },
  {
   "s": 73.34,
   "e": 76.202,
   "text": "But a harness makes them work better,"
  },
  {
   "s": 76.242,
   "e": 77.839,
   "text": "so if you want to productionize"
  },
  {
   "s": 77.879,
   "e": 79.651,
   "text": "an agentic financial workflow,"
  },
  {
   "s": 79.691,
   "e": 81.004,
   "text": "it's a no-brainer."
  },
  {
   "s": 81.055,
   "e": 83.337,
   "text": "The harness is the loop around the model:"
  },
  {
   "s": 83.377,
   "e": 85.578,
   "text": "it gets the context, builds the call,"
  },
  {
   "s": 85.618,
   "e": 88.457,
   "text": "simulates it, then commits, and if anything fails,"
  },
  {
   "s": 88.497,
   "e": 91.157,
   "text": "it goes back and reads again."
  },
  {
   "s": 91.607,
   "e": 94.179,
   "text": "First, context instantiation."
  },
  {
   "s": 94.219,
   "e": 97.233,
   "text": "Reading chain state and wallet state is deterministic,"
  },
  {
   "s": 97.273,
   "e": 98.893,
   "text": "so it doesn't need intelligence."
  },
  {
   "s": 98.933,
   "e": 101.656,
   "text": "It can basically be shrunk to a software function,"
  },
  {
   "s": 101.696,
   "e": 104.907,
   "text": "so what took Claude a dozen"
  },
  {
   "s": 104.947,
   "e": 107.468,
   "text": "calls is one call for the model."
  },
  {
   "s": 107.718,
   "e": 109.791,
   "text": "Then transaction construction."
  },
  {
   "s": 109.831,
   "e": 111.962,
   "text": "The model just says what to call."
  },
  {
   "s": 112.002,
   "e": 113.576,
   "text": "The harness builds the bytes,"
  },
  {
   "s": 113.616,
   "e": 116.525,
   "text": "and its protocol skills already know the rules,"
  },
  {
   "s": 116.565,
   "e": 119.636,
   "text": "like Aave wanting wstETH,"
  },
  {
   "s": 119.676,
   "e": 122.469,
   "text": "or Kamino needing a reserve refresh."
  },
  {
   "s": 122.509,
   "e": 125.576,
   "text": "Those are the things Claude had to learn by failing."
  },
  {
   "s": 129.026,
   "e": 131.006,
   "text": "Those same failures still happen here,"
  },
  {
   "s": 131.046,
   "e": 134.717,
   "text": "but they happen on a fork, before anything is sent."
  },
  {
   "s": 136.367,
   "e": 139.566,
   "text": "Every call runs against a fork of live state first."
  },
  {
   "s": 139.606,
   "e": 140.414,
   "text": "When it reverts,"
  },
  {
   "s": 140.454,
   "e": 143.258,
   "text": "the error comes back to the model as back pressure,"
  },
  {
   "s": 143.298,
   "e": 145.87,
   "text": "and only a green run gets committed."
  },
  {
   "s": 145.91,
   "e": 149.028,
   "text": "It's the same idea as CI for coding agents:"
  },
  {
   "s": 149.068,
   "e": 151.176,
   "text": "tests push back when something breaks,"
  },
  {
   "s": 151.216,
   "e": 153.574,
   "text": "so the model writes good code."
  },
  {
   "s": 158.225,
   "e": 159.543,
   "text": "Once everything passes,"
  },
  {
   "s": 159.583,
   "e": 162.899,
   "text": "Aomi compresses the sequence into one transaction:"
  },
  {
   "s": 162.939,
   "e": 165.348,
   "text": "a smart wallet bundle on Ethereum,"
  },
  {
   "s": 165.388,
   "e": 168.112,
   "text": "one versioned transaction on Solana."
  },
  {
   "s": 168.152,
   "e": 170.085,
   "text": "That saves gas and settlement time,"
  },
  {
   "s": 170.125,
   "e": 172.043,
   "text": "and the model does less."
  },
  {
   "s": 172.993,
   "e": 175.24,
   "text": "And the key never goes to the model."
  },
  {
   "s": 175.28,
   "e": 178.549,
   "text": "Commit hands your wallet a signable transaction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 178.589,
   "e": 179.629,
   "text": "and you sign it,"
  },
  {
   "s": 179.669,
   "e": 182.508,
   "text": "or a scoped session or an agent wallet"
  },
  {
   "s": 182.548,
   "e": 184.907,
   "text": "signs within the limits you set."
  },
  {
   "s": 185.16,
   "e": 190.014,
   "text": "On Solana, a Swig role enforces those limits onchain."
  },
  {
   "s": 192.265,
   "e": 195.406,
   "text": "Then the chain settles it like any other transaction,"
  },
  {
   "s": 195.446,
   "e": 197.426,
   "text": "and Aomi checks the result against"
  },
  {
   "s": 197.466,
   "e": 199.906,
   "text": "the simulation you approved."
  },
  {
   "s": 202.756,
   "e": 205.282,
   "text": "Performance, token efficiency, and security."
  },
  {
   "s": 205.322,
   "e": 207.146,
   "text": "That's what the harness adds."
  },
  {
   "s": 207.796,
   "e": 209.672,
   "text": "The model interprets the intent,"
  },
  {
   "s": 209.712,
   "e": 211.332,
   "text": "your wallet holds the key,"
  },
  {
   "s": 211.372,
   "e": 214.833,
   "text": "and Aomi facilitates everything in between."
  }
 ],
